# Needs the display build: flutter build apk --debug --dart-define=PROBE_AGENT=true --dart-define=PROBE_FIXTURE_WIDGETS=display (see the README).
# What each test shows is also in docs/compat/MATRIX.md: a matrix cell is set only from a test that ran.
# A text selector matches a widget's whole text or any part of it, exactly: case and spaces count (see the negative variants).

before each test
  restart the app
  # the last widget of the screen: right after a restart the agent can answer while the screen is still being built (issue #793)
  wait until "Taps: 0" appears

test "a plain Text is seen by its whole text, a part of it, and contains"
  see "Order total: 42.00"
  see "42.00"
  see "Order total" contains "42.00"

test "the spans of a Text.rich are matched as one text, and each span as a part of it"
  see "Hello world"
  see "Hello"
  see "world"
  see "Hello world" contains "world"

test "the spans of a RichText are matched as one text, and each span as a part of it"
  see "Painted rich text"
  see "rich text"
  see "Painted rich text" contains "rich text"

# What a user sees is cut ("Shipping address: 1600 Amphitheatre…"), but the selector matches the widget's whole string, the cut part included:
# `see` checks the text the app gave the widget, not what was painted.
test "a Text cut with an ellipsis is matched by its whole string, the part that is not painted included"
  see "Shipping address: 1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, California, United States of America"
  see "United States of America"
  see "Shipping address" contains "United States of America"

test "every widget of the screen is found by its id"
  see #wf_text
  see #wf_ellipsis
  see #wf_rich
  see #wf_richtext
  see #wf_icon
  see #wf_image
  see #wf_avatar
  see #wf_logo

# Widgets without text (docs/compat/NEXT.md, item 3). No text on this screen holds "Favorite", "Logo" or "AB", so each match below comes
# from the widget itself. A semantic label is a text selector: when no visible text matches, the agent falls back to a Semantics label
# (an Icon and an Image put their semanticLabel in one), as it does to a Tooltip message for an icon button. The widget found that way
# reads as its label (issue #818; before the fix it read as "").
test "an Icon and an Image are found by their semantic label"
  see "Favorite"
  see "Logo"

test "an Icon and an Image read as their semantic label"
  see "Favorite" contains "Favorite"
  see "Logo" contains "Logo"

test "a CircleAvatar is found and read by its text"
  see "AB"
  see "AB" contains "AB"

test "tap on a FlutterLogo by its id reaches the GestureDetector around it"
  see "Taps: 0"
  tap #wf_logo
  see "Taps: 1"

# Below the fold: a 1200 dp space and then one widget. A ListView builds only the children near the viewport, so the widget is not in the tree until a scroll reaches it.
test "a text below the fold is not seen until a scroll reaches it, and scroll up comes back"
  don't see "Bottom text"
  scroll down until "Bottom text" appears
  see "Bottom text: end of the list"
  scroll up until "Order total: 42.00" appears
